Dear Hiring Team,

I am applying for the *Production Engineer (University Grad)* role at *Meta*. With more than three years building production backend systems and a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, I bring the coding, Linux-oriented systems mindset, and operational discipline to help own services that must remain reliable, performant, and scalable.

At Sperse, I own and productionize a Python/FastAPI multi-agent CRM backend serving 10,000+ users, routing work across 40+ specialized agents with tenant-aware access control. I architected durable workflow services with Temporal and Redis, then debugged long-running executions using progress telemetry, retries, and resumable state. I also wrote and reviewed production code for an MCP service exposing 160+ validated backend actions, and built GitHub Actions CI/CD pipelines with OpenTelemetry trace-based evaluations that assess latency, tool-call accuracy, and production reliability before deployment. This is directly aligned with Meta's need for engineers who establish end-to-end system ownership, write high-quality code, and solve difficult production problems.

Previously at Qualitest, I designed a Java/Spring Boot storage service backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, supporting reliable file operations across S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO. I optimized PostgreSQL using indexes, materialized views, and window functions, and improved error recovery for 100K+ weekly executions through AWS Step Functions and Lambda. Together with my distributed-systems orchestration project, this work has taught me to compare implementation tradeoffs, optimize for performance and scalability, and communicate operational context clearly across engineering work.

Meta's mission to give people the power to build community and bring the world closer together resonates with the responsibility of creating technology that serves people at global scale. I would be excited to contribute to reliable infrastructure and product services while using AI-assisted development responsibly, with measurable quality and safety reviews. Thank you for your consideration; I welcome the opportunity to discuss how I can support Meta's Production Engineering team.

